# The resume lives at /hereismyresume: a fully readable path with no random
# characters — obscurity, not access control, and not enumerated by a
# scanner trying /resume, /cv, /about (see CLAUDE.md). A bare /resume must
# not exist or redirect anywhere. To keep the real path out of search
# results anyway, every response for it carries X-Robots-Tag — this is the
# only way to mark the PDF noindex, since a PDF can't carry a <meta> tag.
# The HTML page also repeats this via a <meta name="robots"> tag in
# src/pages/hereismyresume.astro.
#
# NOTE: the @astrojs/cloudflare adapter injects its own immutable
# Cache-Control block for /_astro/* at the top of this file during
# `astro build` (see astro:build:done in @astrojs/cloudflare) — it prepends
# rather than overwrites, so this file's own rules below are preserved as-is
# on every build. Don't reorder this file expecting it to stay put.
/hereismyresume
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, noai, noimageai

/hereismyresume.pdf
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, noai, noimageai
